I hardly think he'd take it to a disco for Mike to bash away at.

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:16.290
Be careful, Mike.

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:19.090
Oh, don't worry, Jake. Mike likes drums, but then likes people.

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:20.170
My dear, I'm one.

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:22.080
You sure this is the right way to do it?

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:25.180
Yeah, well, according to Elizabeth, it's the way they do it in Africa.

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:27.540
And it's working.

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:30.000
It's the only way I can see to get it properly tuned.

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:32.060
If you want me to play it tonight.

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:39.380
You've never been to a disco before.

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:42.790
Er, no, no, I haven't, actually, Elizabeth.

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:44.940
Not sure I'd enjoy it very much, either.

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:48.130
Well, how do you know? Unless you try, you may have the time of your life.

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:49.710
I hardly think so.

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:53.460
Anyway, you're the only one who can tell us if Mike's drum is the heart of Sogoth one.

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:58.350
The sacrifices one is called upon to make in the line of duty.

00:17:58.350 --> 00:17:59.960
Very well, Elizabeth.

00:18:00.190 --> 00:18:01.510
I'll come to your disco.

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:09.090
Does the music have to be so loud?

00:18:09.090 --> 00:18:09.940
What?

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:12.740
I said, does the music have to be so loud?

00:18:12.740 --> 00:18:15.150
It has to be loud so people can enjoy it.

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:18.650
I always thought one enjoyed music for its melody, not for its volume.

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:19.950
Pop music is different.

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:21.650
Yeah, well, you can shout that again.

00:18:21.650 --> 00:18:25.520
Pop music is perfect.

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:27.700
When's Mike's group coming on?

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:30.000
And now, boy persons and girl persons.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.380
the big moment you've been waiting for,

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:33.280
a brand new group to play for you,

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:34.700
the Hearts of Soggers.

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:36.140
Give them a big welcome.

00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:38.200
The Hearts of Soggers.

00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:40.880
Hearts of Soggers?

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:47.010
That's the drum, all right.

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:48.920
What's Jake think he's playing at?

00:19:50.860 --> 00:19:55.150
doing trying to do a gig if you don't mind let's get on with it Elizabeth why

00:19:55.150 --> 00:20:00.000
are you playing the heart of Sogoth the heart of Sogoth that

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:04.040
an old African drum. He makes a nice primitive sound. We thought we might use it in a couple

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:07.560
of numbers. Why did you let him introduce you as the hearts of Sogoth? You're the fresh

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:11.580
hearts and always have been. The hearts of Sogoth? Elizabeth, what are you talking about?

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:15.340
He didn't say that. You've got Sogoth or Soggy or whatever it is on the brain, Elizabeth.

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:19.020
You can't interfere with a group like this. What are you doing to Mike, to the fresh hearts,

00:20:19.020 --> 00:20:22.260
to the group? I'm trying to manage them. Now, if you don't mind, we'll get on with the

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:25.000
sense. Mike!

00:20:30.090 --> 00:20:30.610
about, Elizabeth.

00:20:31.650 --> 00:20:32.550
Sock of business.

00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:33.570
I had to stop this.

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:35.710
What sock of business?

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:39.630
With the music, the drums, everyone going mad.

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:43.210
The only person who's going mad around here is you, Elizabeth.

00:20:43.890 --> 00:20:45.820
Jaunting on the stage like that.

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:49.400
Lucky everyone was enjoying themselves too much to notice.

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:52.300
The drum, the fear.

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:55.140
Feeling all right, Elizabeth?

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:57.510
No, I'm going back to the lab.

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:00.000
Right, but don't go jaunting again in public.

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:11.450
you are worried Elizabeth something is troubling you it's nothing Tim that is

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:17.790
not true please tell me I've started imagining things or something I feel I'm

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:25.040
going mad imagining what sort of things well at the disco tonight Mike started

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:30.000
to play a drum an African drum called the heart of soggeth and then everyone's

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:37.400
started chanting, Sogoth, Sogoth, like that. Then they all seem to go into a sort of a

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:42.860
trance. But Mike says it didn't happen, and that he's never heard the word Sogoth before.

00:21:43.470 --> 00:21:46.670
Well, even John says he's never heard of the heart of Sogoth, yet he went to one of

00:21:46.670 --> 00:21:54.110
their meetings. Now he says it didn't happen. It did happen, Elizabeth. John did go to a

00:21:54.110 --> 00:22:00.000
meeting of the Sogoth sect. There is a drum called the heart of Sogoth, and Mike did play

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:03.500
play it at the concert you and John went to tonight.

00:22:03.500 --> 00:22:07.030
That's a weight off my mind. I wasn't imagining it.

00:22:07.030 --> 00:22:07.530
Then why--

00:22:07.530 --> 00:22:12.350
Why was John lying? And Mike as well?

00:22:12.350 --> 00:22:14.970
Well, there can only be one reason.

00:22:14.970 --> 00:22:18.470
Tim, I think they've been taken over in some way.
